            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_191N2010D">
               <eventList type="performances" xml:id="eventList_201762d9">
                  <event xml:id="event_d1e458450">
                     <date isodate="1860-03-19" xml:id="date_f2aadcbb">1860-03-19</date>
                     <geogName role="venue" xml:id="geogName_191N20194">Vor Frue Kirke</geogName>
                     <geogName role="place" xml:id="geogName_191N20198">Copenhagen</geogName>
                     <persName role="" xml:id="persName_191N2019F">J.P.E. Hartmann, organ</persName>
                     <desc xml:id="desc_25accaec">First performance.</desc>
                  </event>
               </eventList>
               <p xml:id="idm99">Nicolai Peter Nielsen (1795-1860) was a Danish actor famous for his interpretation of the heroes in Oehlenschläger's dramas. He and his wife, the actress Anna Nielsen, were close friends of Hartmann and his wife. They had both performed in his melodramas. N.P. Nielsen was also active as an actor outside Denmark, such as at Burgtheater in Vienna.</p>
            </history>
